course: dictionary
lesson: 12731
title: Dreamlike
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dreamlike is a describing word. It is made from dream and like, so it means "like a dream". Something dreamlike feels strange, soft or unreal, as if you were half asleep. «The mist rolled over the hills in a dreamlike haze.» The mist is not really a dream, but it looks and feels like one.
explain: The word can also mean very beautiful and peaceful, the kind of thing you might dream of. «The moon shone on the still lake, and the whole night was dreamlike.» The clues around the word tell you which meaning fits: strange and unreal, or calm and lovely.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in the words "like a dream". If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. Try it with «The music was dreamlike» and see what happens.
fact: Dreamlike means like a dream.
fact: «Dreamlike» means strange, soft or unreal, as if it were happening in a dream.
fact: «Dreamlike» can also mean very beautiful and peaceful.
fact: Writers often use dreamlike for mist, moonlight, music or odd events that do not feel real.
fact: In «Alice's Adventures», the story has a dreamlike feel, and at the end we learn it was all a dream.
exercise: «The mist rolled over the hills in a dreamlike haze.» What does dreamlike mean? | Very loud and noisy | *Strange, soft and unreal, like a dream | Wet and cold like a river | Quick and busy
exercise: «The music was dreamlike and calm, and we felt peaceful.» What does dreamlike mean here? | Fast and noisy | Loud and angry | Dirty and wet | *Very beautiful and peaceful, like a dream
exercise: Can you swap "like a dream" for dreamlike in «The scene by the lake was dreamlike»? | No, it means the lake is dirty | No, it becomes a question about a shop | Yes, but it becomes a shout | *Yes, the sentence still makes sense
test: «The moonlit village looked dreamlike in the mist.» What does dreamlike mean? | Hungry and tired | Short and rude | *Strange and unreal, like a dream | Bright and noisy
test: Which thing is most likely to be dreamlike? | A sunny chess match in a noisy hall | A bus timetable | *Music drifting across a misty lake at night | A bag of wet sand
exam: Which is the best meaning of dreamlike? | Wet and grey | Very hungry | *Like a dream: strange, soft, unreal, or very peaceful | Short and rude
